NAMES — a memory that won’t answer
FORMAT (LOCKED)

Duration: 25 seconds
Aspect Ratio: Flexible (9:16 or 16:9 both valid)
Tempo Feel: Slow, uncounted pulse (≈ 60–70 BPM felt, not explicit)
Color Language: Muted, low saturation; grayscale drifting toward sepia
Texture: Soft analog grain, constant, barely perceptible

CORE CONSTRAINTS (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

❌ No narrative resolution
❌ No performance energy
❌ No climax
❌ No explicit storytelling

✅ Everything feels unfinished
✅ Silence is as important as sound
✅ Emotion leaks indirectly, never stated

EMOTIONAL EXTRACTION (THE CORE)
Theme: Names as ghosts — labels without bodies
Emotion: Tender detachment, quiet ache, emotional under-articulation
Perspective: Someone remembering after caring has already faded
Mood Curve: Still → slightly heavier → still again
No catharsis. No confession. Just residue.

AUDIO STRUCTURE (ABSTRACT, NON-MUSICAL)
Bed: One sustained harmonic field (soft organ / filtered pad / bowed tone)
Slight pitch drift (±5 cents), slow breathing modulation
Motif: Sparse, single-note gestures
Appear → vanish → never repeat the same way

Voice Presence:
Treated as texture, not lead
Whisper-adjacent, distant, partially obscured
No intelligible lyrics required — breath + shape only

Negative Space:
Audible gaps
Moments where nothing happens and that is the point

VISUAL LOGIC (MINIMALIST CINEMA)
Static or near-static frames with micro-motion only
curtain shifting
light flicker
camera breathing imperceptibly

Objects over people:
paper with names
empty rooms
windows, doorframes, mirrors

If a human appears:
Never fully visible
Back turned, cropped, or partially out of frame

TEMPORAL FLOW (25s)

0–6s
Stillness. Environment establishes emotional temperature.
Sound barely arrives.

6–14s
A name feels spoken (or almost).
Subtle emotional weight increases — not louder, just closer.

14–20s
Maximum density — still quiet.
This is the emotional center, but it refuses to bloom.

20–25s
Elements thin out.
Nothing resolves.
The memory stays open.

WORLD LOGIC (LOCKED)
Names do not summon people
Memory does not guarantee feeling
Intimacy can exist without presence
Meaning is implied, never delivered

FINAL NOTE (CWWP INTENT)
This vignette should feel like:
finding a name in your handwriting
and not remembering who it belonged to
but feeling that it once mattered